  <div id="sutta">
  
              <h2 id="SN1.71" class="h1">Having Killed<br/>
                Chetvā Sutta  (SN 1:71)</h2>
              <p>As she was standing to one side, a devatā recited this verse to the Blessed One:</p>
              <div class="verse">
                <p>“Having killed what</p>
                <p class="v1">do you sleep in ease?</p>
                <p>Having killed what</p>
                <p class="v1">do you not grieve?</p>
                <p>Of the slaying</p>
                <p>of what one thing</p>
                <p class="v1">does Gotama approve?”</p>
                <div class="verse-add">
                  <p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
                  <p>“Having killed anger</p>
                  <p class="v1">you sleep in ease.</p>
                  <p>Having killed anger</p>
                  <p class="v1">you do not grieve.</p>
                  <p>The noble ones praise</p>
                  <p>the slaying of anger</p>
                  <p class="v1">—with its honeyed crest</p>
                  <p class="v1">&amp; poison root—</p>
                  <p>for having killed it</p>
                  <p class="v1">you do not grieve.”</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../MN/MN21.html">MN 21</a>; <a href="SN7_2.html">SN 7:2</a>; <a href="../AN/AN7_60.html">AN 7:60</a></p>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
